{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_xKp9I6sWjWVPmyxagIxc9566","tool":"record_mapping","input":{"mapping_type":"routine","id":"0x8212","name":"GameEngine - per-frame dispatch on GameMode ($0770)","length":6,"notes":"The game-mode dispatch. Runs once per frame from the NMI: at CPU $8175 the NMI does JSR $8212, guarded by LDA $0776 / LSR A / BCS (skip) at $816F-$8173, so it only runs when OperMode bit 0 is clear. Entry $8212: LDA $0770 (GameMode) ; JSR $8E04 (jump engine), and the 4-entry target table follows at $8218: $8231 (mode 0 = title screen / attract demo), $AEDC (mode 1 = game / in a level), $838B (mode 2 = victory), $9218 (mode 3 = game over). $8E04 is the jump engine: ASL A / TAY / PLA / STA $04 / PLA / STA $05 / INY / LDA ($04),Y / STA $06 / INY / LDA ($04),Y / STA $07 / JMP ($0006) - it pops the return address (the table at $8218) and uses A as a byte index to fetch the target and JMP indirectly. Both $8231 and $AEDC are themselves secondary dispatchers (each starts LDA $0772 / JSR $8E04). Found with no reference by searching PRG for LDA $0770: the only match in the per-frame path is $8212, which the NMI calls. Emulator proof: play_input/watch on $0770 read 0 on the title/attract screen and flipped to 1 exactly when the second Start began World 1-1; the mapping's LoseLife sets $0770=3 at game over, which is mode 3 -> $9218. Table bytes at $8218: $8231,$AEDC,$838B,$9218.","source":"trace and disassembly","rom_origins":[{"mem":"prgRom","offset":8210,"length":6,"notes":"$8212 LDA $0770 / JSR $8E04; table at $8218 = prgRom 0x218"}]}}
