{"type":"text","text":"Done. Both routines are found, proven, recorded, and the six confirmed discoveries are promoted to the ROM's mapping file.\n\n## 1. Game-mode dispatch — entry `$8212`\n\n**What it does:** the per-frame switch that picks the title / in-level / victory / game-over handler.\n\n```\n$8212: AD 70 07   LDA $0770        ; GameMode\n$8215: 20 04 8E   JSR $8E04        ; JumpEngine\n$8218: 31 82      .dw $8231        ; mode 0 = title screen / attract demo\n$821A: DC AE      .dw $AEDC        ; mode 1 = game (in a level)\n$821C: 8B 83      .dw $838B        ; mode 2 = victory\n$821E: 18 92      .dw $9218        ; mode 3 = game over\n```\n\n`$8E04` (JumpEngine) is `ASL A / TAY / PLA / STA $04 / PLA / STA $05 / INY / LDA ($04),Y / STA $06 / INY / LDA ($04),Y / STA $07 / JMP ($0006)` — it pops its return address (the table at `$8218`) and indexes it with the mode.\n\n**Evidence**\n- The NMI calls it every frame at `$8175`: `LDA $0776 / LSR A / BCS skip / JSR $8212`.\n- Found by searching PRG for `AD 70 07` (`LDA $0770`); `$8212` is the match in the per-frame path.\n- Emulator: watching `$0770` while pressing Start read **0** on the title/attract screen and flipped to **1** exactly when the second Start began World 1-1; the known `LoseLife` sets `$0770=3`, which is mode 3 → `$9218` (game over).\n\n## 2. Area palette loader — entry `$85BF`\n\n**What it does:** at level start, chooses which of four 32-byte palette blocks the NMI copies to the PPU.\n\n```\n$85BF: AC 4E 07   LDY $074E        ; area palette index\n$85C2: BE BB 85   LDX $85BB,Y      ; selector table $85BB = 01 02 03 04\n$85C5: 8E 73 07   STX $0773        ; queue the VRAM/palette transfer\n$85C8: 4C 45 87   JMP $8745\n```\n\nThis is **step 9** of the level-init state machine at `$8567` (`LDA $073C / JSR $8E04`, table at `$856D`). The NMI then does (`$80B6`–`$80C3`) `LDX $0773 / LDA $805A,X / STA $00 / LDA $806D,X / STA $01 / JSR $8EDD`; `$8EDD`/`$8E92` is the actual hardware writer — `STA $2006` (`=$3F`) / `STA $2006` (`=$00`) then `LDA ($00),Y / STA $2007` ×32 — loading all 4 BG + 4 sprite palettes at once from the selected PRG records `$8CA4` (1), **`$8CC8` (2, overworld / 1-1)**, `$8CEC` (3), `$8D10` (4), each `[3F 00 20 <32 bytes> 00]`.\n\n**Evidence**\n- `trace_writes` **read** on the selector table `$85BB` during a forced 1-1 reload (time-up death) returned exactly one access: PC `$85C5` (after `LDX $85BB,Y`), address `$85BC` = `$85BB + $074E` with `$074E=1`, value **2**.\n- `trace_writes` read over `$8CA0`–`$8D27` during another reload caught the NMI writer reading `$8CC8`–`$8CEB` (PCs `$8E96/$8E9C/$8EBB/$8EE2`) into `$2007`.\n- Direct test: writing `$0773=1` while paused then `step_frame 1` swapped the entire level to the `$8CA4` palette (pipes turned blue/pink, ground green — screenshot); `$0773=2` restored the normal overworld colours. The live 1-1 palette matches the `$8CC8` block exactly.\n- `$074E` read 1 during World 1-1 play.\n\n**Recorded** (source `trace and disassembly`): routine `$8212` (GameEngine), routine `$85BF` (LoadAreaPalette), plus the supporting hardware writer `$8EDD` (WriteVRAMBuffer), addresses `$074E`/`$0773`, and the `level_start_palette_chain` note. `promote_mappings` wrote all six into the ROM's mapping file."}
